    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0399" n="1213" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg1213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman
                    file</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Special Assistant to the President
                        for National Security Affairs (Cutler) to the Chairman of the United States
                        Atomic Energy Commission (Strauss)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d105-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-09-10">September 10, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I had a talk this morning with the President about various matters brought up at
                    the Council Meeting yesterday.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d105-f2"/> His mind turned
                    again, as it has very frequently, to the thermonuclear device explosion on
                    August 12.</p>
                <pb facs="0400" n="1214" xml:id="pg1214"/>
                <p>He said that he would like you to estimate in your opinion what this explosion
                    might mean in the capability of the Soviets to produce such devices in the next
                    two or three years, assuming that they have a capability as good as our best
                    capability.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Cutler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
